          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Seth P. Waxman, congress amended the Organic Act of Guam to replace the Ninth Circuit\u2019s certiorari jurisdiction with direct review by this Court, but the amendment did not specify whether it applies to cases already pending before the Ninth Circuit."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 8,
              "start": 8
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Court issued an order withdrawing and deferring a ruling in this case pending the decision in the related Santos case."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Seth P. Waxman",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0fc92376d6feec09a75ccc39d5eaa0a31be2484f3e978e1d7923e4ab2bfb7104",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0000-0000",
              "ev-0fc92376d6fe-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The parties ask whether the amendment\u2019s language and purpose require it to apply to pending appeals, and what the proper definition of \u201ctax valuation\u201d is for Guam tax purposes."
      }
    ],
